# Never bake an operator's .env into an image layer. apps/api is bind-mounted
# over /app at runtime (compose), so the real .env is always read from the host
# there - baking a copy only ships secrets inside the image and makes the build
# fail on whatever a hand-edited .env happens to contain (an unquoted value, a
# stray CRLF). The build itself needs no .env: `artisan package:discover` runs
# against composer's manifest, not configuration.
apps/api/.env
apps/api/.env.*
!apps/api/.env.example
